        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summarize the Production Shift"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZE_THE_PRODUCTION_SHIFT",
          "id": "1764877669158",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764877669159_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## context\nOperator Notes are general comments written by an Operator in the Manufacturing industry about events that occurred during their work shift at a Workstation. \nProduction Exceptions are issues that have occurred and have a resolution for all Workstations within a Workcenter for the given shift. \nSupervisor Comments are hand-off notes entered by the supervisor at the end of the shift. \n\nWhere inputs are not present, do not add details or bring new facts to the response. Just respond with \"The supervisor has not left any specific comments\" or \"The absence of operator notes means I can't provide any highlights\".\n\n## operator notes\n {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OperatorNotes}} \n\n## production exceptions\n {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProductionExceptions}} \n\n## supervisor comments\n {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.SupervisorComments}} '''{supervisor_comments}'''\n\n## instructions\nUsing the operator notes, production exceptions, and supervisor comments above, answer the following questions. Do not add any information that is not provided as input. \n\nWhat are the key highlights of things that went well during the work shift (Highlights)?\n\nWhat are the key highlights of things that need attention that occurred during the work shift (Needs Attention)?\n\nWhat are the comments that the supervisor provided about the shift (Comments)? \n\n## output formatting\nOutput in bullet point format.\n\nOutput in the third person point of view.\n\nUse neutral language.\n\nOutput in less than 250 words.\n\nDo not use bold section headings.\n\nRemember not to add details that were not in the original inputs."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
